{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"MCP ENDPOINT IS BACK. `/mcp` returns 401 (auth required) rather than 502 — the upstream is answering. Total outage roughly 18:31 PDT 09-02 to 06:41 PDT 09-03, about 12 hours.\n\nRecovery came from the prerequisite bug `febd-6b13-1976-43be`: change 2558 pinned uv in the container images, which restored the ability to BUILD, and the next autodeploy tick then rebuilt and cut over. Journal at 06:41:01: 'mcp cutover complete: /mcp upstream now 127.0.0.1:8092 (deploy DONE)'. `docker ps` shows `rebar-mcp-3e04025b684e-8092 Up (healthy)` and the nginx upstream now names that live port instead of the dead 8093.\n\n## THIS TICKET IS NOT DONE — recovery is not the fix\n\nThe endpoint is up, but every acceptance criterion on this ticket is about the system SURVIVING and DETECTING this, and none of that changed:\n\n- **AC(a) — reachable during/after long async gate jobs.** Unaddressed. The container was OOM-killed roughly 3 minutes into a plan-review run on an 8 GiB box. Nothing about that has changed; the next long gate can repeat it.\n- **AC(b) — unhealthy upstream detected and reported.** Still entirely missing. There is no `mcp_healthy` metric (confirmed via `list-metrics` on rebar/host); `observability.sh` probes only Gerrit and the review-bot; the container's own `/health` is not routed by any nginx location; and the deploy declares success at the flip without re-validating. For ~12 hours nothing in the system could observe that /mcp was down — a human reported it.\n- **AC(c) — regression test or operational probe for upstream loss during a gate.** Still missing.\n\nAlso still standing, and worth its own attention: the `mcp_retire_sweep` guard in autodeploy.sh reaps an exited-but-live container while nginx still names its port (the live-backend `continue` sits only inside the `Running=true` branch), which is how a transient crash becomes a permanent 502.\n\nRecording this explicitly so 'the 502 cleared' is not mistaken for the bug being fixed — the same trap this project hit on 3276, where growing the volume was nearly recorded as the resolution."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788417928346575001,"uuid":"d1484281-bfe9-4fad-a241-b1b738ad16a1"}